      "id": "LicenseRef-W3C-Document-License",
      "basis": "The document's own copyright paragraph, under its header: \"Copyright © 2016-2024 World Wide Web Consortium. W3C® liability, trademark and W3C Document License rules apply.\", where 'W3C Document License' links to the W3C Document License (https://www.w3.org/copyright/document-license/; no SPDX id). It permits copying and distributing the document's contents, or portions of them, in any medium for any purpose, provided every copy carries a link to the original, the pre-existing copyright notice, and the document's status; it grants NO right to modify. So this entry holds the text verbatim and changes no wording: the link, notice and status are on its first two page sections (page-001, page-002) and repeated in `note`. Splitting it into per-page files is a reading of 'portions' and of 'any medium', recorded here so the owner can overrule it, as for w3c-2013-prov-o (issue #1614).",
      "note": "Source: uploads/w3c-2024-prov-jsonld-submission.pdf (sha256 ab826cd4a4cfe750c6b7eac6a8439b21c1114af747e3a1a05f48de7b4472c230, 71 pages), a browser print (Chrome 154 / Skia PDF, created 2026-10-01) of the HTML specification; every page carries the print's running header and footer ('10/1/26, 6:17 PM', 'The PROV-JSONLD Serialization', 'https://www.w3.org/submissions/prov-jsonld/', 'N/71'), which are NOT stripped because the page rung has no such option. The printed URL is the latest-version URL; the document's own header identifies the text as 'W3C Member Submission 25 August 2024', 'This version: https://www.w3.org/submissions/2024/SUBM-prov-jsonld-20240825/', 'Latest published version: https://www.w3.org/submissions/prov-jsonld/', editors Luc Moreau and Dong Huynh (King's College London). It was not compared byte for byte with the w3.org copy. The PDF carries no outline, so it was ingested with the pdf-pages rung: one section per PAGE, no chapter tree inferred (bean 6xaz). In this print each heading's '§' self-link text is extracted at the END of the page the heading is on, not at the heading's position. NOTICE: The PROV-JSONLD Serialization: A JSON-LD Representation for the PROV Data Model, W3C Member Submission 25 August 2024, https://www.w3.org/submissions/2024/SUBM-prov-jsonld-20240825/. Copyright © 2016-2024 World Wide Web Consortium. W3C® liability, trademark and W3C Document License rules apply. Status: a W3C Member Submission (submitted by King's College London), acknowledged but NOT endorsed by W3C — its status section reads: \"By publishing this document, W3C acknowledges that the Submitting Members have made a formal Submission request to W3C for discussion. Publication of this document by W3C indicates no endorsement of its content by W3C, nor that W3C has, is, or will be allocating any resources to the issues addressed by it. This document is not the product of a chartered W3C group, but is published as potential input to the W3C Process.\""
